-- הסכם קיבוצי מיום 18.12.01 (הסתדרות המורים) — הסכם השכר לעובדי הוראה
-- לתקופה שמיום 1.1.99 ועד ליום 31.12.01: the wage agreement of the
-- 1999–2001 round between the teachers' employers — the State, the Centre
-- of Local Government for the local authorities, and the three large cities
-- — and הסתדרות המורים. Its period and whom it covers (§§2–3); the one-time
-- grant of 1,250 for 1999–2000 (§4); the 3% wage supplement on the combined
-- salary from 1.1.01, "תוספת 2001" (§5); the shekel supplements updated by
-- 3.6% (§6); the supervision, instruction and teacher-instructor allowances
-- of annex א (§7); the special-education supplement (§8); the seminaries'
-- promotion grades (§9); the negotiation over 0.306% of the cost and the
-- 0.2% table update that follows if it fails (§10); the negotiation over the
-- final cost of 1.8.01–31.12.01 (§11); disputes, exhaustion, industrial
-- peace, earlier agreements, the follow-up committee and when it is paid
-- (§§12–17).
--
-- WHO CITES IT: §6 of the agreement of 21.2.2008 exhausts its §11 (printing
-- "11.12.01", finding F-hh-2008-b there) and imports this file; the takanon
-- names it as the source of §1.1ב's 3%, §4.6's special-education rates and
-- the allowance tables of §§8.1–8.4 — §§8.3 and 8.4 take their tables'
-- rates from its annex א, which they import. The takanon's sections are
-- held to it in l4/tests/2001-12-18_histadrut-hamorim_wage-agreement-1999-2001-tests.l4.
-- The 2011 framework's "תוספת 2001" is the general public-sector agreement
-- of 31.1.01's 3.6%, not this agreement's 3%, and stays the framework's.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT budget_foundations_law

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — הסכם השכר לעובדי הוראה לתקופה 1.1.99–31.12.01 (הסתדרות המורים, 18.12.2001)`

DECLARE `2001 wage agreement action` IS ONE OF
    `act to apply the 2001 wage agreement to the owners' teaching employees`
    `pay the 2001 one-time grant to a teacher who left before the signing`
    `act with the local authorities to find the teachers owed the 2001 grant`
    `show the 2001 wage supplement on its own payslip line`
    `act to recognise the 2001 wage supplement as fixed for the pensions law`
    `decide the special-education supplement of a teacher no group of §8 names`
    `negotiate the 0.306% of the 2001 agreement's cost`
    `negotiate the final cost of 1.8.01–31.12.01`
    `strike over a matter the 2001 wage agreement settled`
    `decide a dispute over the 2001 wage agreement`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The registration stamp: registered on 15.4.2002, number 7006/2002; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 "Between"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The State and who represents it (the wages commissioner and the Ministry's Director-General); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p6 The Centre of Local Government, for the local authorities save the three large cities; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p7 The three large cities (Jerusalem, Tel Aviv, Haifa); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 The employers' short name, "on the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 "And"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 הסתדרות המורים and its secretary-general; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 The union's short name, "on the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p12 A recital: the parties negotiated the teachers' wage agreement for 1.1.99–31.12.2001.
-- akn:preamble/p13 A recital: a one-time grant for 1999–2000, a supplement for 1999–2001, and a negotiation over the final cost, as set out below.
-- akn:preamble/p14 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

-- ¶3: made and signed on 18.12.01.
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the 2001 wage agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 18 12 2001

§§ `1 המבוא והנספחים`

@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_1/p1
`the 2001 wage agreement's preamble and annexes are part of it` MEANS TRUE

§§ `2 תקופת ההסכם`

@ref akn:art_2 akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the 2001 wage agreement's period` d IF
        d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1999)
    AND d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2001)

§§ `3 תחולת ההסכם`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as the agreement of 18.12.01 asks.
DECLARE `2001 wage agreement teacher` HAS
    `in the teaching scale, for the 2001 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by one of the 2001 agreement's employers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the State, a local authority the Centre of Local Government signed for, or one of the three large cities
    `employed by an owner, for the 2001 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc an owner (בעלות) the State supervises and budgets
    `on a sabbatical in the 2001 agreement's period` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 3.1: every teaching-scale employee of the employers ("עובדי הוראה");
-- 3.3: a teacher on a sabbatical in all or part of the period too.
@ref akn:art_3 akn:art_3__para_3-1 akn:art_3__para_3-3
GIVEN t IS A `2001 wage agreement teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 wage agreement applies to` t IF
        t's `in the teaching scale, for the 2001 agreement`
    AND t's `employed by one of the 2001 agreement's employers`

-- 3.2: the State acts to apply it to the owners' teaching employees too, as
-- the one that supervises and budgets them: a duty to act, not coverage.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2
`applying the 2001 wage agreement to the owners' teachers` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `act to apply the 2001 wage agreement to the owners' teaching employees`

§§ `4 מענק חד פעמי`

-- 4.1.1: a teacher employed in 1.1.99–31.12.2000, or part of it, is owed a
-- one-time grant of 1,250, a pensioner too; ¶2: paid with the salary of
-- January 2002 and no later than February 2002 (§17 says the same).
@ref akn:art_4 akn:art_4__para_4-1 akn:art_4__para_4-1__subpara_4-1-1 akn:art_4__para_4-1__subpara_4-1-1/p2
`the 2001 one-time grant` MEANS 1250

GIVEN `months employed in 1999–2000` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owed the 2001 one-time grant` `months employed in 1999–2000` IF
    `months employed in 1999–2000` GREATER THAN 0

GIVEN m IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 grant may be paid with the salary of` m IF
        m `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2002)
    AND m `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2002)

-- 4.1.2: an employer other than the State pays the grant to one who was
-- dismissed or resigned, not into a pension, before the signing, within 30
-- days of his asking; the Centre of Local Government works with the local
-- authorities to find them.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-1__subpara_4-1-2
`paying the grant to a teacher who left before the signing` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2001 one-time grant to a teacher who left before the signing`
    WITHIN 30

`finding the teachers owed the grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `act with the local authorities to find the teachers owed the 2001 grant`

-- 4.2: the grant is for 1999 and 2000, spread evenly over their 24 months,
-- by the position and the share of the two years employed; ¶2: it is no
-- wages commissioner's approval under §29 of the Budget Foundations Law
-- (imported) of any departure in pay concerning the position.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2
GIVEN `months employed in 1999–2000` IS A NUMBER, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 one-time grant owed` `months employed in 1999–2000` `position fraction` IS
    `the 2001 one-time grant` TIMES `position fraction` TIMES (min 24 `months employed in 1999–2000`) DIVIDED BY 24

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2/p2
`the 2001 grant is a §29 approval of a departure in the position` MEANS FALSE

-- 4.3: a budgetary pensioner gets it too, by his pension rate and the
-- months of 1999 and 2000 he received a pension.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3
GIVEN `pension rate` IS A NUMBER, `months on pension in 1999–2000` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 one-time grant a pensioner is owed` `pension rate` `months on pension in 1999–2000` IS
    `the 2001 one-time grant` TIMES `pension rate` TIMES (min 24 `months on pension in 1999–2000`) DIVIDED BY 24

-- 4.4: it does not change the salary base of the table on the eve of the
-- signing. 4.5: it is not salary for any purpose, not counted for
-- severance or the hour value, nor for a study fund, a provident fund, an
-- accruing pension fund or managers' insurance. 4.7: nor for the
-- completion to the minimum wage (the Minimum Wage Law is outside the
-- corpus).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4 akn:art_4__para_4-5 akn:art_4__para_4-7
DECLARE `what the 2001 payments might count for` IS ONE OF
    `the 2001 table's salary base`
    `severance pay, for the 2001 agreement`
    `the hour value, for the 2001 agreement`
    `a study fund, for the 2001 agreement`
    `a provident fund, for the 2001 agreement`
    `an accruing pension fund or managers' insurance, for the 2001 agreement`
    `the completion to the minimum wage, for the 2001 agreement`
    `percentage supplements on the combined salary, for the 2001 agreement`
    `pensions, for the 2001 agreement`
    `the Dafna fund, for the 2001 agreement`

GIVEN p IS A `what the 2001 payments might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 one-time grant counts for` p IF FALSE

`why the Minimum Wage Law is not in the 2001 agreement` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שכר מינימום, התשמ\"ז-1987"

-- 4.6: the grant does not exhaust the union's claims to change the
-- supplement's rate for 1.8.01–31.12.01 (§11).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-6
`the 2001 grant exhausts the claims for 1.8.01–31.12.01` MEANS FALSE

§§ `5 תוספת שכר`

-- 5.1: from 1.1.01, a wage supplement of 3% of the combined salary ("תוספת
-- השכר").
@ref akn:art_5 akn:art_5__para_5-1
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 wage supplement rate on` d IS
    IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001) THEN 3% ELSE 0

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 wage supplement` d `combined salary` IS
    `the 2001 wage supplement rate on` d TIMES `combined salary`

-- 5.2: on its own line of the payslip.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-2
`showing the 2001 supplement on its own line` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `show the 2001 wage supplement on its own payslip line`

-- 5.3: salary for every purpose — percentage supplements on the combined
-- salary, the hour value, severance (the Severance Pay Law), pensions,
-- pension contributions, the study fund, the Dafna fund and every other
-- contribution or deduction customary for the combined salary. 5.5: but
-- for the grades it lists, not for the minimum-wage completion.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-3
GIVEN p IS A `what the 2001 payments might count for`, `in a grade 5.5 lists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 wage supplement counts for` p `in a grade 5.5 lists` IF
    IF p EQUALS `the completion to the minimum wage, for the 2001 agreement`
    THEN NOT `in a grade 5.5 lists`
    ELSE NOT (p EQUALS `the 2001 table's salary base`)

`why the Severance Pay Law is not in the 2001 agreement` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק פיצויי פיטורים, התשכ\"ג-1963"

-- 5.4: the State acts to recognise it as a fixed supplement for the State
-- Service (Pensions) Law (outside the corpus).
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-4
`recognising the 2001 supplement for pension` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `act to recognise the 2001 wage supplement as fixed for the pensions law`

`why the State Service (Pensions) Law is not in the 2001 agreement` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שירות המדינה (גמלאות) [נוסח משולב], התש\"ל-1970"

-- 5.5: the grades whose supplement is left out of the minimum-wage
-- completion: certified kindergarten teacher, certified teacher, senior
-- teacher, the three intermediate grades, B.A. and M.A. only.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-5
DECLARE `2001 salary grade` IS ONE OF
    `certified kindergarten teacher, 2001 grade`
    `certified teacher, 2001 grade`
    `senior teacher, 2001 grade`
    `intermediate grade A, 2001 grade`
    `intermediate grade B, 2001 grade`
    `intermediate grade C, 2001 grade`
    `B.A., 2001 grade`
    `M.A., 2001 grade`
    `another grade, for the 2001 agreement`

GIVEN g IS A `2001 salary grade`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a grade 5.5 lists` g IF
    NOT (g EQUALS `another grade, for the 2001 agreement`)

-- 5.6: 5.5 is no precedent and no ground for a like demand elsewhere.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-6
`5.5 is a precedent for other agreements` MEANS FALSE

§§ `6 עדכון תוספות שכר שקליות`

-- From 1.1.2001 every shekel supplement paid in the teaching scale on the
-- eve of the signing is updated by 3.6%, save (א) one with an updating
-- mechanism of its own, not by the cost-of-living agreements; (ב) the
-- completion to the minimum wage; (ג) the one-time grant and expense
-- refunds.
@ref akn:art_6 akn:art_6/p1 akn:art_6__para_a akn:art_6__para_b akn:art_6__para_c
DECLARE `shekel payment of 2001` HAS
    `updated by the cost-of-living agreements, for 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a minimum-wage completion, for 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the grant or an expense refund, for 2001` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN s IS A `shekel payment of 2001`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§6 of 2001 updates the shekel payment` s IF
        s's `updated by the cost-of-living agreements, for 2001`
    AND NOT s's `a minimum-wage completion, for 2001`
    AND NOT s's `the grant or an expense refund, for 2001`

GIVEN s IS A `shekel payment of 2001`, `amount on the eve` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shekel payment as §6 of 2001 updates it` s `amount on the eve` d IS
    IF `§6 of 2001 updates the shekel payment` s AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001)
    THEN `amount on the eve` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.6%)
    ELSE `amount on the eve`

§§ `7 גמול פיקוח, גמול הדרכה וגמול מורה מדריך`

-- ¶1: from 1.1.01 the supervision, instruction and teacher-instructor
-- allowances are raised to the rates of annex א, by years of seniority in
-- supervision or instruction. Annex א: the supervisor 65.5% at year 1 up
-- to 95.5% at year 13, the instructor 47.5% up to 70.5%, the
-- teacher-instructor 43% at every year. The table stops at 13 years — the
-- seniority ceiling the takanon's §§8.3.6.3 and 8.4.6.3(ד) put on the
-- count ("כפוף לתקרה - כיום 13 שנה") — so its last row is the rate from then on, and
-- less than a full year reads as the first row (an exception to convention
-- thresholds.missing-row, with that reason).
@ref akn:art_7 akn:art_7/p1 akn:attachments akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/t1
DECLARE `2001 supervision role` IS ONE OF
    `a supervisor, for the 2001 annex`
    `an instructor, for the 2001 annex`
    `a teacher-instructor, for the 2001 annex`

`the 2001 annex's supervisor column` MEANS
    LIST 65.5%, 68%, 70.5%, 74.5%, 76.5%, 79%, 81%, 83.5%, 86%, 88.5%, 91%, 93.5%, 95.5%
`the 2001 annex's instructor column` MEANS
    LIST 47.5%, 49.5%, 51%, 53%, 54.5%, 56.5%, 58.5%, 60%, 62%, 63.5%, 66%, 68%, 70.5%

GIVEN r IS A `2001 supervision role`, `years of seniority in supervision or instruction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 annex rate for` r `years of seniority in supervision or instruction` IS
    IF r EQUALS `a teacher-instructor, for the 2001 annex`
    THEN 43%
    ELSE at (IF r EQUALS `a supervisor, for the 2001 annex`
             THEN `the 2001 annex's supervisor column`
             ELSE `the 2001 annex's instructor column`)
            (`the row of the 2001 annex for` `years of seniority in supervision or instruction`)
    WHERE
        `the row of the 2001 annex for` n MEANS (min 13 (max 1 (FLOOR n))) MINUS 1

GIVEN r IS A `2001 supervision role`, n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 annex applies on` r n d IF
    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001)

-- ¶2: the annex's rates exhaust every provision on those rates in
-- agreements, arrangements and practice — among them the agreements of
-- 16.11.83, 15.5.89 and 19.9.1994 and the circular of 27.9.95 (none of
-- them in the corpus).
@ref akn:art_7/p2
`the 2001 annex exhausts the earlier supervision rates` MEANS TRUE

`why the earlier supervision agreements are not in the 2001 agreement` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "ההסכמים מיום 16.11.83, 15.5.89 ו־19.9.1994 וחוזר הביצוע מיום 27.9.95"

§§ `8 תוספת חינוך מיוחד`

-- 8.1: a special-education teacher certified for it (as the circulars it
-- names define, or the Ministry defines in consultation with the unions),
-- from 1.1.2001: 14% of the combined salary in place of 10% in a
-- special-education kindergarten, school or institution, a מפת"ן or a
-- special-education class in a regular school; 9% in place of 7% as an
-- integration teacher in regular education. 8.2: one not certified: 8.5%
-- in place of 6.5%, and 5.5% in place of 3.5%. 8.3: these replace every
-- earlier arrangement.
@ref akn:art_8 akn:art_8__para_8-1 akn:art_8__para_8-1/p2 akn:art_8__para_8-1/p3 akn:art_8__para_8-2 akn:art_8__para_8-2/p2 akn:art_8__para_8-2/p3 akn:art_8__para_8-3
DECLARE `2001 special-education setting` IS ONE OF
    `a special-education setting, for 2001`
    `integration in regular education, for 2001`
    `no setting §8 of 2001 names`

GIVEN s IS A `2001 special-education setting`, certified IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 special-education supplement rate` s certified d IS
    BRANCH IF s EQUALS `a special-education setting, for 2001` AND `from 1.1.2001`
              THEN (IF certified THEN 14% ELSE 8.5%)
           IF s EQUALS `integration in regular education, for 2001` AND `from 1.1.2001`
              THEN (IF certified THEN 9% ELSE 5.5%)
           IF s EQUALS `a special-education setting, for 2001`
              THEN (IF certified THEN 10% ELSE 6.5%)
           IF s EQUALS `integration in regular education, for 2001`
              THEN (IF certified THEN 7% ELSE 3.5%)
           OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        `from 1.1.2001` MEANS d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001)

`why the special-education circulars are not in the 2001 agreement` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוזרי מנכ\"ל מיוחד ה', לג/1, לב/8, מיוחד ד' וחוזר אגף כוח אדם בהוראה מיום 1.1.92"

-- 8.4: the follow-up committee decides the supplement of an entitled
-- special-education teacher in no group of 8.1–8.2.
@ref akn:art_8__para_8-4
`deciding an ungrouped special-education supplement` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MAY   `decide the special-education supplement of a teacher no group of §8 names`

§§ `9 דרגות קידום בסמינרים ומכללות`

-- Out of this agreement's cost the seminaries' agreement of 22.5.97 is
-- amended as set out in an agreement of the same day, 18.12.01; neither is
-- in the corpus.
@ref akn:art_9 akn:art_9/p1
`why the seminaries' agreements are not in the 2001 agreement` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "הסכם הסמינרים והמכללות להכשרת עובדי הוראה מיום 22.5.97, ותיקונו בהסכם מיום 18.12.01"

§§ `10 המשך משא ומתן`

-- 10.1: a negotiation over applying 0.306% of the teachers' wage cost, out
-- of this agreement's cost, 0.106% of it for the teachers' welfare.
-- 10.2: the remaining 0.2% the same for every teaching-scale employee; with
-- no agreement by 31.3.2002, the combined salary table rises by 0.2% from
-- the salary of April 2002, back to 1.1.2001, and that exhausts 10.1 save
-- the 0.106%.
@ref akn:art_10 akn:art_10__para_10-1 akn:art_10__para_10-2
`negotiating the 0.306%` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `negotiate the 0.306% of the 2001 agreement's cost`

`the 2001 agreement's cost to be negotiated` MEANS 0.306%
`the part of it for the teachers' welfare` MEANS 0.106%

GIVEN `agreed by 31.3.2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 table update if no agreement` `agreed by 31.3.2002` IS
    IF `agreed by 31.3.2002` THEN 0 ELSE `the 2001 agreement's cost to be negotiated` MINUS `the part of it for the teachers' welfare`

#ASSERT `the 2001 table update if no agreement` FALSE EQUALS 0.2%

GIVEN `agreed by 31.3.2002` IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 0.2% update is in force on` `agreed by 31.3.2002` d IF
        NOT `agreed by 31.3.2002`
    AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001)

§§ `11 קביעת עלות סופית`

-- The parties negotiate the final cost for 1.8.01–31.12.01. §6 of the
-- agreement of 21.2.2008 exhausts this clause (that file imports this one).
@ref akn:art_11 akn:art_11/p1
`negotiating the final cost of 1.8.01–31.12.01` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `negotiate the final cost of 1.8.01–31.12.01`

`the period whose final cost §11 of 2001 leaves open starts on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2001

§§ `12–16 סכסוכים, מיצוי, שקט, הסכמים קודמים וועדת מעקב`

-- §12: every collective dispute declared by the signing on the matters
-- settled here is void with it.
@ref akn:art_12 akn:art_12/p1
GIVEN `declared on` IS A DATE, `on a matter this agreement settled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a labour dispute is void under the 2001 wage agreement` `declared on` `on a matter this agreement settled` IF
        `on a matter this agreement settled`
    AND `declared on` `is on or before` `the 2001 wage agreement was signed on`

-- §13: a full exhaustion, nationally and locally, of the claims on the
-- matters settled here for 1.1.99–31.07.01, and no further negotiation on
-- them. The months after are §11's.
@ref akn:art_13 akn:art_13/p1
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `on a matter this agreement settled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 wage agreement exhausts the claim for` d `on a matter this agreement settled` IF
        `on a matter this agreement settled`
    AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1999)
    AND d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 2001)

-- §13's exhaustion ends the day before §11's open period starts.
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL `the period whose final cost §11 of 2001 leaves open starts on` EQUALS (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 2001) PLUS 1)

-- §14: from the signing to 31.12.2001, neither side strikes or locks out
-- on the matters settled here.
@ref akn:art_14 akn:art_14/p1
`industrial peace under the 2001 wage agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    SHANT `strike over a matter the 2001 wage agreement settled`

-- §15: earlier terms stand for its period unless it amends or cancels them.
@ref akn:art_15 akn:art_15/p1
`earlier terms stand unless the 2001 wage agreement changes them` MEANS TRUE

-- §16: a joint parity follow-up committee — the wages commissioner, the
-- union's secretary-general, the Ministry's Director-General and a local
-- government representative — follows it and decides disputes unanimously;
-- its decisions are final and bind the parties.
@ref akn:art_16 akn:art_16/p1 akn:art_16/p2
`deciding disputes over the 2001 wage agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MAY   `decide a dispute over the 2001 wage agreement`

-- akn:art_16/p3 A fax banner; no rule.

§§ `17 מועדי התשלום`

-- The further payments and the differences are paid from the salary of
-- January 2002 and at the latest with that of February 2002.
@ref akn:art_17 akn:art_17/p1
GIVEN m IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 differences may be paid with the salary of` m IF
    `the 2001 grant may be paid with the salary of` m

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 The signing formula; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The signatures; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/t1 The parties signing; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p3 A stamp of a human-resources director; no rule.

§§ `examples`

-- A full-time teacher employed throughout 1999–2000: the whole 1,250; one
-- employed half the time at half a position: 312.50.
#ASSERT `the 2001 one-time grant owed` 24 1 EQUALS 1250
#ASSERT `the 2001 one-time grant owed` 12 0.5 EQUALS 312.5
#ASSERT `the 2001 one-time grant a pensioner is owed` 0.7 24 EQUALS 875
#ASSERT `the 2001 grant may be paid with the salary of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2002)
#ASSERT NOT `the 2001 grant may be paid with the salary of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2002)
#ASSERT NOT `the 2001 one-time grant counts for` `the hour value, for the 2001 agreement`
#ASSERT `the 2001 wage supplement counts for` `the hour value, for the 2001 agreement` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the 2001 wage supplement counts for` `the completion to the minimum wage, for the 2001 agreement` TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2001 wage supplement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001) 10000 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the 2001 wage supplement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2000) 10000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2001 annex rate for` `a supervisor, for the 2001 annex` 1 EQUALS 65.5%
#ASSERT `the 2001 annex rate for` `an instructor, for the 2001 annex` 13 EQUALS 70.5%
#ASSERT `the 2001 annex rate for` `a supervisor, for the 2001 annex` 20 EQUALS 95.5%
#ASSERT `the 2001 annex rate for` `a teacher-instructor, for the 2001 annex` 7 EQUALS 43%
#ASSERT `the 2001 special-education supplement rate` `a special-education setting, for 2001` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001) EQUALS 14%
#ASSERT `the 2001 special-education supplement rate` `integration in regular education, for 2001` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2000) EQUALS 3.5%

`a cost-of-living-linked shekel payment of 2001` MEANS
    `shekel payment of 2001` WITH
        `updated by the cost-of-living agreements, for 2001` IS TRUE
        `a minimum-wage completion, for 2001` IS FALSE
        `the grant or an expense refund, for 2001` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the shekel payment as §6 of 2001 updates it` `a cost-of-living-linked shekel payment of 2001` 100 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001) EQUALS 103.6
#ASSERT `a labour dispute is void under the 2001 wage agreement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2001) TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2001 wage agreement exhausts the claim for` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2001) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the 2001 wage agreement exhausts the claim for` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2001) TRUE

`a teacher of a local authority, for the 2001 agreement` MEANS
    `2001 wage agreement teacher` WITH
        `in the teaching scale, for the 2001 agreement` IS TRUE
        `employed by one of the 2001 agreement's employers` IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner, for the 2001 agreement` IS FALSE
        `on a sabbatical in the 2001 agreement's period` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the 2001 wage agreement applies to` `a teacher of a local authority, for the 2001 agreement`
